    "result_text": "Done. The full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 2/2 tests passing, 0 failures).\n\n## What I changed\n\nThe `locality` field is a read-time derived value on the owner, exactly like the existing `membershipTier` \u2014 so I followed that pattern rather than inventing a new OfficeFloor step:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `locality` property to the `Owner` schema (readOnly, derived), so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added `@Mapping(target = \"locality\", qualifiedByName = \"locality\")` and a `@Named(\"locality\")` method backed by a fixed `CITY_REGION` table (`Sydney\u2192NSW`, `Melbourne\u2192VIC`, `Brisbane\u2192QLD`), returning `\"UNKNOWN\"` for any other city.\n\nBecause `locality` is computed at read time in the mapper (which `RespondWithOwner` already uses for `GET /api/owners/{id}`), no YAML pipeline or new function class was needed. The two acceptance tests \u2014 known city `Sydney \u2192 NSW` and a random unknown city \u2192 `UNKNOWN` \u2014 both pass.",
