    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe `locality` mapping slots in exactly alongside the existing derived-field pattern in `OwnerMapper` (`displayName`, `initials`, `membershipTier`): a `@Mapping(... qualifiedByName = \"locality\")` on `toOwnerDto` plus a matching `@Named(\"locality\")` default method. That is the right unit for a read-time derived field \u2014 this interface is already the home for owner\u2192DTO derivations, so nothing new is being invented and the class isn't being stretched beyond its existing responsibility.\n\nThe lookup table lives as an interface constant next to the method that uses it, the logic isn't duplicated anywhere, and the `getOrDefault(..., \"UNKNOWN\")` cleanly expresses the spec's fallback in one line. The OpenAPI `locality` property mirrors the shape of the neighboring `membershipTier`/derived fields (`readOnly: true`, example, description), so the contract and the mapper stay in step. A maintainer of this file would find it natural.\n\n(Non-blocking: the inline `java.util.Map` FQNs could be imports to match the rest of the file, but that's cosmetic and doesn't affect the structural soundness of the change.)",
